-DOM so a rebuilt list yields a different node than the held reference.
+- A NEW `@conformance` scenario, `The completion-toggle seams do not rebuild the list on a
+  same-visibility toggle`, guards the invariant at the SOURCE level: `completeTodo` and
+  `toggleAllTodos` must mutate the toggled `<li>` in place and must not rebuild the list when the
+  item stays visible. This is the source-level conformance check for the browser-only defect: the
+  happy-dom harness cannot exercise a real browser's detach, so a structural guard is the durable
+  backstop that survives a rebuild of the app code. QM implements the structural check (bespoke
+  parser or ast-grep over `js/app.js`) as verification support.
